# AI project development guide

1. **Read first:** open and follow repo-root `AI_PROJECT_DEVELOPMENT_REFERENCE.md` end-to-end for the request. Treat the generated `<!-- PLANNING_STANDARD:* -->` block and `src/utils/projectPlanningStandard.ts` as the SoT for shared product meaning (structure limits, publishing checklist, instruction levels, cross-cutting rules). Treat §A / §B field catalogs as the SoT for SQL/authoring columns.
2. **Build out a project (§H):** phrases like "ref ai dev guide and build out project X" or "Build out content for project X ref ai dev guide" are a **complete** instruction - run §H end to end without asking which steps, phases, or deliverable. Owned phases only on catalog templates (standard and linked/adopted phases are read-only there). When the user explicitly asks to build out **standard phases** / **Standard Foundation**, author on the foundation project instead (H.1 exception). Audit every in-scope step, author in §H.3 order, bootstrap the shared tools/materials library as needed. **Draft** one SQL file per guide step while developing; **before commit**, concatenate into one `<slug>_<scope>_bundle.sql`, delete the per-step drafts, then **commit, push, and name the migration path(s) in the final report** (§H.5). Missing the push or the migration handoff is an incomplete build out.
3. **Field catalogs in §B / §D–§F are required** for project catalog work - use the listed columns/JSON keys; verify names against `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` and `src/interfaces/Project.ts` before writing SQL or content.
4. **Home maintenance (§G):** when the request is about `maintenance_templates` / home maintenance task lists, follow **§G** (schema/UI fit, criticality levels, industry research protocol, system gating, idempotent SQL). Research standards before changing frequencies or guidance.
5. **Continuous improvement (standard changes only):**
   - Using this guide to author or ship catalog content / migrations does **not** update the guide or planning standard. Rules stay fixed until a real standard change is needed.
   - If a **shared product** rule changes (structure, checklist, instruction levels, cross-cutting meaning), update `src/utils/projectPlanningStandard.ts`, then run `npm run sync:planning-standard` (and confirm with `npm run check:planning-standard`). Do not hand-edit the marker block in the markdown.
   - If a durable **SQL / field / authoring** lesson changes how future work must be done, append a dated **Revision history** row in `AI_PROJECT_DEVELOPMENT_REFERENCE.md` and fold the rule into the matching §A–§H section. Do not log ordinary project build-outs or content migrations there.
